// Package io reads the program's standard input. Stdout and stderr are
// written with fmt.
//
// A line ends at "\n"; a "\r" directly before it is removed too. The last
// line is returned even if it has no "\n". readLine and readAll share one
// buffer, so they can be mixed. Calls from different goroutines are
// serialised, and each call gets whole lines. Stdout is flushed before
// stdin is read. Reading is a stop point: a goroutine whose group is
// stopped while it waits for input stops there.
package io

// The next line of stdin without its line ending, or null at end of input.
// The error is set only when reading fails, not at the end.
pub fn readLine() (string?, error)

// Everything left on stdin, up to end of input ("" if nothing is left).
pub fn readAll() (string, error)
